  "model_slug": "ptec-6643-vav-pressure-dependent-hot-water",
  "short_model": "PTEC Pressure Dependent VAV 6643",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6643",
    "Application 6643",
    "App 6643",
    "550-496PA",
    "Siemens pressure dependent VAV"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Pressure-dependent VAV terminal unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Pressure-dependent VAV boxes with one or two hot water reheat valves, run on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller 550-496PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6643 runs a pressure-dependent VAV box (no airflow sensor) with hot water reheat on a Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller over BACnet MS/TP. The cooling loop modulates the supply air damper directly; in heating the box gets its minimum airflow from a mechanical stop and the heating loop modulates one or two reheat valves, which can be sequenced, in parallel or overlapping.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "There is no airflow measurement in this application; minimum airflow comes from a mechanical stop on the box.",
    "VALVE CNT (AO 88) sets whether one or two reheat valves are used; VLV 1/VLV 2 START and END set their share of the heating loop."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Conditioner - VAV Pressure Dependent with Hot Water Heat, Application 6643, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1170",
    "revision_date": "2014-07-17",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/O1Wa40I37Qs0ownBRhdbNA/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the box to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, and reads room temperature, damper and reheat valve position and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 49",
        "name": "DMPR POS",
        "why": "Supply air damper position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 53",
        "name": "VLV 1 POS",
        "why": "Reheat valve 1 position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6691."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The controller keeps all associated equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely."
    ]
  },
